%% Sequence view 1 — happy path (read-only return)
%% This mirrors the actual span tree emitted by `python run.py run "<question>"`.
%% Span names in the notes are the real ones, so a reviewer can diff the diagram
%% against `prototype/runs/<id>/trace.jsonl`.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant IG as Input guardrail
    participant ORC as Orchestrator
    participant CP as Checkpoint store
    participant W1 as Worker 1
    participant W2 as Worker 2
    participant T as Tools (search/fetch/summarize)
    participant RG as Retrieved-content guardrail
    participant M as Model (small / large)
    participant CTX as Context assembler
    participant OG as Output guardrail
    participant GR as Groundedness screen
    participant OT as OTel

    User->>IG: question
    Note over OT: span orchestrator.research_run opens (trace root)
    IG->>IG: injection / scope / PII screen
    IG-->>OT: span guardrail.input (allowed=true)
    IG->>ORC: allowed

    ORC->>M: decompose (tier=small)
    M-->>ORC: subquestions[1..N], N ≤ 3
    ORC-->>OT: span model.plan (tokens, cost_usd)
    ORC->>CP: commit checkpoint "plan"

    ORC->>ORC: project cost vs per-task ceiling
    Note right of ORC: over ceiling → cap width + downgrade routing<br/>(never silently overspend)

    par fan-out (bounded, parallel — wall-clock = slowest worker)
        ORC->>W1: subquestion 1
        W1->>T: search(query, max_results)
        T-->>W1: candidate sources
        W1->>T: fetch(url)  [https + allowlist enforced]
        Note over T: transport: fixture (default) or real HTTP —<br/>robots.txt, HTML→text, size cap, post-DNS address check
        T-->>W1: document
        W1->>RG: screen retrieved text
        RG-->>W1: sanitised text (instruction-like spans neutralised)
        W1->>T: summarize(document_id, focus)
        T->>M: extractive summary (tier=small)
        M-->>T: summary
        T-->>W1: summary + citation metadata
        W1-->>ORC: evidence[]
        ORC->>CP: commit checkpoint "worker:0"
    and
        ORC->>W2: subquestion 2
        W2->>T: search / fetch / summarize
        Note over T: fetch is deduped per URL —<br/>two workers wanting one source pay once
        W2-->>ORC: evidence[]
        ORC->>CP: commit checkpoint "worker:1"
    end
    W1-->>OT: span worker.retrieval.0 (+ child tool spans)
    W2-->>OT: span worker.retrieval.1

    ORC->>CTX: assemble(question, plan, evidence, failed=[])
    CTX-->>ORC: payload (60% evidence / 20% plan / 20% headroom,<br/>≤2 summaries per sub-question — lever L3)
    Note right of CTX: raw documents are NOT in the payload —<br/>only ranked extractive summaries + citations

    ORC->>M: synthesize (tier=large)
    M-->>ORC: report_markdown, covered[], coverage_gaps[]
    ORC-->>OT: span model.synthesize (largest cost_usd in the trace)
    ORC->>CP: commit checkpoint "synthesis"

    ORC->>OG: report
    OG->>OG: every claim cited? PII? instruction leak?
    OG-->>OT: span guardrail.output (citation_rate=1.0)
    OG->>CP: commit checkpoint "guardrail:output"

    OG->>GR: report + fetched source texts
    GR->>GR: per claim: content coverage, numeric grounding,<br/>invented negation — against the CITED source's text
    GR-->>OT: span guardrail.groundedness (claims_checked, claims_unsupported)
    Note right of GR: the source text comes from retrieved memory, not the<br/>summary — checking against a model-written summary<br/>would test internal consistency, not grounding
    GR->>CP: commit checkpoint "guardrail:groundedness"
    GR-->>User: cited, verified report (READ path — no confirmation needed)

    Note over OT: root span closes with run.cost_usd, run.fanout_width;<br/>on-call can answer "what did this run do and why" from the tree alone
